<!-- Main Content Area -->
<div class="md:col-span-6 space-y-24">
<!-- Daily Care Section -->
<section class="scroll-mt-32" id="daily-care">
<div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8">
<div class="h-12 w-1 bg-heritage-crimson"></div>
<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-on-surface">Daily Care</h2>
</div>
<div class="grid gap-6">
<div class="bg-white border border-outline-variant/30 p-8 rounded-xl hover:border-heritage-crimson/20 transition-all duration-300">
<h3 class="font-label-sm text-label-sm uppercase text-heritage-crimson mb-2">Preservation</h3>
<p class="font-body-md text-on-surface mb-4">Athangudi tiles are cured with natural oils. For daily cleaning, use a soft-bristled broom or a micro-fiber dust mop to prevent abrasive grit from scratching the polished surface.</p>
<div class="bg-surface-cream p-4 rounded-lg flex gap-3 italic text-on-surface-variant font-body-md text-sm border-l-4 border-architectural-blue">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined">lightbulb</span>
<span>Always dry-mop before any wet cleaning to remove loose particles that act like sandpaper.</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<!-- Deep Cleaning Section -->
<section class="scroll-mt-32" id="deep-cleaning">
<div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8">
<div class="h-12 w-1 bg-heritage-crimson"></div>
<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-on-surface">Deep Cleaning</h2>
</div>
<div class="bg-white border border-outline-variant/30 overflow-hidden rounded-xl">
<div class="p-8">
<p class="font-body-md text-on-surface-variant mb-6">When tiles lose their luster or require a more thorough wash (bi-weekly), follow the pH-neutral protocol.</p>
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
<div class="p-6 bg-surface-container-lowest border border-outline-variant/10 rounded-lg">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-architectural-blue mb-2">water_drop</span>
<h4 class="font-semibold text-on-surface mb-2">Neutral Cleansers</h4>
<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">Use only pH-neutral soaps. Avoid acidic cleaners (lemon, vinegar) which eat into the cement.</p>
</div>
<div class="p-6 bg-surface-container-lowest border border-outline-variant/10 rounded-lg">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-architectural-blue mb-2">opacity</span>
<h4 class="font-semibold text-on-surface mb-2">Drying Protocol</h4>
<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">Never allow water to air-dry. Wipe excess moisture immediately with a clean, dry cotton cloth.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<!-- Stain Removal (Bento Grid Style) -->
<section class="scroll-mt-32" id="stain-removal">
<div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8">
<div class="h-12 w-1 bg-heritage-crimson"></div>
<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-on-surface">Artisanal Stain Remedies</h2>
</div>
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
<div class="bg-surface-cream p-8 rounded-xl border border-heritage-crimson/10 col-span-2">
<h3 class="font-label-sm text-label-sm uppercase text-heritage-crimson mb-4">Oil &amp; Grease Stains</h3>
<div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 items-start">
<div class="flex-1">
<p class="font-body-md mb-4 text-on-surface-variant">Because Athangudi tiles are porous, oil can penetrate deep. Use the traditional 24-hour Baking Soda Poultice for best results.</p>
<ol class="space-y-2 text-sm text-on-surface-variant">
<li class="flex gap-2"><span class="font-bold text-heritage-crimson">01.</span> Mix baking soda with water to a toothpaste consistency.</li>
<li class="flex gap-2"><span class="font-bold text-heritage-crimson">02.</span> Apply a 1cm thick layer over the stain.</li>
<li class="flex gap-2"><span class="font-bold text-heritage-crimson">03.</span> Cover with plastic wrap and let sit for 24 hours.</li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="w-full md:w-32 h-32 bg-white rounded-lg border border-outline-variant flex items-center justify-center">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-outline-variant">science</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="bg-white p-6 border border-outline-variant/30 rounded-xl">
<h4 class="font-semibold text-architectural-blue mb-2">Red Wine/Coffee</h4>
<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">Blot immediately. Do not rub. Clean with a solution of water and a few drops of hydrogen peroxide.</p>
</div>
<div class="bg-white p-6 border border-outline-variant/30 rounded-xl">
<h4 class="font-semibold text-architectural-blue mb-2">Ink &amp; Dyes</h4>
<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">Use a cotton ball soaked in rubbing alcohol. Tap gently until the ink is lifted into the cotton.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<!-- Sealing Schedule -->
<section class="scroll-mt-32" id="sealing">
<div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-8">
<div class="h-12 w-1 bg-heritage-crimson"></div>
<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-on-surface">Professional Sealing</h2>
</div>
<div class="relative overflow-hidden p-8 bg-architectural-blue text-white rounded-xl">
<div class="relative z-10">
<h3 class="font-headline-md text-white mb-4">Maintaining the Barrier</h3>
<p class="mb-8 opacity-90">Athangudi tiles require periodic resealing to maintain water and stain resistance. Use a high-quality penetrating sealer that allows the cement to breathe.</p>
<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-8">
<div>
<p class="font-label-sm text-secondary-fixed mb-1">Residential</p>
<p class="text-2xl font-display-lg">Every 3-5 Years</p>
</div>
<div class="h-12 w-px bg-white/20 hidden sm:block"></div>
<div>
<p class="font-label-sm text-secondary-fixed mb-1">Commercial</p>
<p class="text-2xl font-display-lg">Every 12-18 Months</p>
</div>
</div>
